qsvdec frames carried the dts of the packet that was being decoded when the
runtime returned them, several packets after their own. When the pts had a
fault (two frames with the same pts, as on an MPEG-2 open GOP whose leading
B-frame repeats the I-frame's pts), guess_correct_pts() switched
best_effort_timestamp to that dts for the rest of the stream, and ffmpeg
played every frame late by the decoder's delay (2 frames on Arc A750 and A380).

Set FF_CODEC_CAP_SETS_PKT_DTS so lavc leaves pkt_dts unset, as it does for
the other asynchronous wrappers (mediacodec, v4l2_m2m, mmal, libopenh264).

diff --git a/libavcodec/qsvdec.c b/libavcodec/qsvdec.c
--- a/libavcodec/qsvdec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/qsvdec.c
@@ -1280,7 +1280,8 @@
     .p.priv_class   = &x##_qsv_class, \
     .hw_configs     = qsv_hw_configs, \
     .p.wrapper_name = "qsv", \
-    .caps_internal  = FF_CODEC_CAP_NOT_INIT_THREADSAFE | FF_CODEC_CAP_EXPORTS_CROPPING, \
+    .caps_internal  = FF_CODEC_CAP_NOT_INIT_THREADSAFE | FF_CODEC_CAP_EXPORTS_CROPPING | \
+                      FF_CODEC_CAP_SETS_PKT_DTS, \
 }; \
 
 #define DEFINE_QSV_DECODER(x, X, bsf_name) DEFINE_QSV_DECODER_WITH_OPTION(x, X, bsf_name, options)
